import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Registering security at the RCCM: what lenders get wrong" description="Security taken over assets in Cameroon is only as good as its registration.">
<div>
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(40px,6vw,88px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(24px,3vw,40px)">
    <a href="/insights/" class="lnk" style="background:none;border:0;padding:0;cursor:pointer;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#007EA7;margin-bottom:32px">← Insights</a>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:3 / span 8;min-width:280px">
        <div style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px;color:#6b7b82;margin-bottom:22px">[month year] · Banking &amp; Finance</div>
        <h1 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(32px,4.4vw,56px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;max-width:26ch">Registering security at the RCCM: what lenders get wrong</h1>
        <div style="font-size:15px;color:#4a5a61;margin:26px 0 0">By <span style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13.5px;color:#6b7b82">[author name, title]</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.14);margin:0" />
  <section style="max-width:1360px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(36px,4vw,56px) clamp(20px,5vw,80px) clamp(56px,7vw,96px)">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));gap:32px">
      <div style="grid-column:3 / span 7;min-width:280px">
        <p style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(19px,1.8vw,23px);line-height:1.6;color:#00171F;margin:0 0 32px;max-width:62ch">Security taken over assets in Cameroon is only as good as its registration. The documents are rarely the problem; the register usually is.</p>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 20px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">The OHADA Uniform Act on Secured Transactions gives lenders a wide menu: pledges of shares, bank accounts, receivables, stock and equipment, assignments by way of security, and the guarantee and counter-guarantee regime. Most of these interests take effect against third parties only once they are entered in the Trade and Personal Property Credit Register — the RCCM — held at the registry of the competent court.</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(23px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:40px 0 16px">Registration is not a formality</h2>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 20px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Signing does not create priority. Where two lenders take security over the same asset, the order of entry in the register ordinarily decides which of them is paid first. A facility that closed on time but registered late can sit behind a competitor that documented the same collateral a month later.</p>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 20px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">Registrations also expire. A registered interest is entered for a period, and a renewal missed during a refinancing or a change of agent leaves the lender unsecured against third parties while the loan is still outstanding. In portfolio reviews this is the single most common defect we find.</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(23px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:40px 0 16px">Three practical points</h2>
        <ol style="margin:0 0 20px;padding-left:22px;max-width:68ch;display:grid;gap:12px">
          <li style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f">Make registration a condition subsequent with a hard date and evidence requirement, not a covenant to use reasonable endeavours.</li>
          <li style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f">Keep a renewal calendar at agent level, not at borrower level, and test it at every amendment.</li>
          <li style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#28383f">Search the register before each drawdown of a revolving facility, not only at closing.</li>
        </ol>
        <h2 style="font-family:Spectral,Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(23px,2.2vw,29px);line-height:1.25;margin:40px 0 16px">Enforcement</h2>
        <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:#28383f;margin:0 0 20px;max-width:68ch;text-wrap:pretty">A properly registered interest opens routes that do not require a full trial on the merits. Those routes are procedural and unforgiving: the notices, time limits and proofs are prescribed, and a step taken out of order can restart the process. Lenders should plan enforcement while documenting the facility, when the borrower is still cooperative and the register is still clean.</p>
        <p style="font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:#6b7b82;margin:40px 0 0;max-width:68ch;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,23,31,0.16);padding-top:20px">This article is general information about Cameroonian and OHADA practice. It is not legal advice, does not address any particular transaction, and no lawyer-client relationship arises from reading it. [Sample article template — final copy, author and date to be supplied by the firm.]</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
